<title>USA: Nationwide says claims from Fran to reach $150 mln.</title>
<headline>Nationwide says claims from Fran to reach $150 mln.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nationwide Insurance Enterprise said Monday revised projections indicate its claims from Hurricane Fran could soar to $150 million.</p>
<p>The company said the hurricane generated more than 33,000 claims calls from its policyholders in eight states. If the current call-in rate continues, the claims volume could go to 50,000 or more, the company added.</p>
<p>Nationwide said the hardest-hit state is North Carolina, where it is the largest property-casualty insurer.</p>
</text>
